From 5507a38228bf6124592b10c880fabd29cb90d741 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:16:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): queued strict links readers share one
 rebuild instead of each projecting in turn

On a board written every few seconds, a strict reader's fingerprint (taken before _links_lock) never matched
the projection it had waited for, so every reader queued on the lock rebuilt in series. Hub observation: 412
strict projections in 57 min at ~6 s wall each, the lock held ~98% of the time, ~12 threadpool workers parked
on it and Desktop user-steps polls timing out at 6-10 s while the hub sat 79% idle.

Readers now take an arrival ticket before fingerprinting and each projection a start ticket before reading any
store. Under the lock, a cached projection that started after the reader arrived answers it: it read every store
after the reader's own writes, so read-your-writes holds. A reader never takes a projection that started before
it arrived. New diag event <lane>.shared counts the reuse.

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
